{"name":"Glowing Brake Disc","hex":"#ee4444","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"glowing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of glow"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The action of glowing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glowing"},{"term":"brake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A device used to slow or stop the motion of a wheel, or of a vehicle, usually by friction (although other resistive forces, such as electromagnetic fields or aerodynamic drag, can also be used); also, the controls or apparatus used to engage such a mechanism such as the pedal in a car. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The act of braking, of using a brake to slow down a machine or vehicle"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To operate a brake or brakes.","To be stopped or slowed (as if) by braking."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brake"},{"term":"disc","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thin, flat, circular plate or similar object.","An intervertebral disc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To harrow with a disc harrow.","To move towards, or operate at, zero blade pitch, orienting the propeller blades face-on to the oncoming airflow and maximizing the drag generated by the propeller."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disc"}],"entries":[{"title":"Disc brake","blocks":[{"text":"A disc brake is a type of brake that uses the calipers to squeeze pairs of pads against a disc to create friction. There are two basic types of brake pad friction mechanisms: abrasive friction and adherent friction. This action slows the rotation of a shaft, such as a vehicle axle, either to reduce its rotational speed or to hold it stationary. The energy of motion is converted into heat, which must be dissipated to the environment. Disc brakes are found in most automobiles and are more expensive to manufacture than a drum brake. Disc brakes are also found on some higher-end bicycles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Disk_brake_dsc03682.jpg/330px-Disk_brake_dsc03682.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disc_brake","wikidata":"Q755174"},{"title":"Brake","blocks":[{"text":"A brake is a mechanical device that inhibits motion by absorbing energy from a moving system. It is used for slowing or stopping a moving vehicle, wheel, axle, or to prevent its motion, most often accomplished by means of friction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Disc_brake.jpg/330px-Disc_brake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brake","wikidata":"Q1534839"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Disk_brake_dsc03682.jpg/500px-Disk_brake_dsc03682.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Disk_brake_dsc03682.jpg/1280px-Disk_brake_dsc03682.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Disk_brake_dsc03682.jpg/500px-Disk_brake_dsc03682.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Close-up of a disc brake on a Renault car","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADisk_brake_dsc03682.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Suspension.jpg/500px-Suspension.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Suspension.jpg/500px-Suspension.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"On automobiles, disc brakes are often located within the wheel","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASuspension.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb